NAME
     sh - the shell

SYNOPSIS
     sh [-c COMMAND] [-i] [FILE]

DESCRIPTION
     sh reads commands and runs them. It is a POSIX-shaped shell: pipes,
     redirection (< > >> 2> 2>&1 <<EOF), && and || and ;, & for the
     background with job control (jobs, fg, bg, kill %1), command
     substitution with $(...) and backticks, variables and $((...))
     arithmetic, globbing, quoting, functions, and the control
     structures if, while, until, for, case and select.

     Built-ins include cd, export, read, test ([ ]), source (.), exec,
     eval, shift, set, unset, trap, wait, umask, ulimit, alias, jobs, fg,
     bg, kill, times, type, getopts, true, false, echo and exit. A login
     shell reads /etc/profile and then ~/.profile.

OPTIONS
     -c COMMAND   run COMMAND and exit
     -i           interactive, whatever the input is
     FILE         read commands from FILE

SEE ALSO
     env(1), test in sh(1) itself, crontab(5)
